    "created_at": "2021-01-19T07:23:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-19T07:49:22Z",
    "body": "One thing I missed when reading through this in 2018 is that \"await a stable state\" is invoked when the algorithm is not running \"in parallel\" (`load()` invokes \"media element load algorithm\" which invokes \"resource selection algorithm\").\r\n\r\nI also don't see where it is invoked while \"in parallel\" (and it also seems that would break down).\r\n\r\nAm I missing something or could we remove the \"Await a stable state\" step here?\r\n\r\nSo 3bb022ce7df6033371f6d2aa407e9ea362d44f0d made invocations \"asynchronous\" (without defining what that means). 566c4f9a74cc7fc745f1f1daf2616e074a16713a undid some of this. I cannot make a whole lot of sense out of going through blame, but it does look like there was a fair amount of confusion and lack of clarity around these concepts.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
