    "created_at": "2021-05-06T12:03:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-06T12:03:49Z",
    "body": "Thanks @padenot! The test added there is here now:\r\nhttps://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource/resource-selection-currentSrc.html?run_id=5677336357765120&run_id=5721877584543744&run_id=5638047716605952&run_id=5718410715463680\r\n\r\nSafari still fails the test, and I've filed https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=225451.\r\n\r\nDoes anything still remain in this issue?\r\n\r\n@annevk you're right that the \"await a stable state\" stuff looks wrong, but originally it was clear enough. It's equivalent to yielding and then continuing to run the following steps at the next microtask checkpoint. As actually implemented these algorithms have to be split into multiple parts, where continuing to run the next part is queued. The spec could be rewritten like that, but wouldn't necessarily be easier to follow.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
